    description: "**Defect.** The language-composition summary presents the repository as an 18-language polyglot, where most of the extra languages come only from test fixtures.\n\n**Evidence.** `profile.languages` reports 18 languages including go/rust/java/csharp/solidity/wgsl/swift, each ~{files:1, loc:~20}, all sourced from tests/fixtures/schema-coverage-corpus/<lang>/. Most of those fixture nodes are flagged is_test_file=True (csharp 6/6, wgsl 5/5, go 7/9, rust 6/9, java 5/6, solidity 7/8, swift 6/7). The application is a Python+TypeScript project. The profile counts every file the analyzer enumerates with no exclusion of test-fixture files.\n\n**Contract.** A \"what is this written in?\" composition summary should reflect the real codebase composition, or document that fixture languages are included. (Note: spec §profile defines languages[L].files as \"count the analyzer would enumerate\" with no test exclusion, so this is per-contract — weak/borderline.)\n\n**Consequence.** A consumer asking what languages the project uses is told it is a 7-extra-language polyglot (incl. Solidity/WGSL/Swift) when those appear only as test fixtures — a misleading picture of the technology stack.\n\n**Related (not duplicate).** Adjacent to INV-nohod (test-dominated node count) but a distinct surface: the codebase-composition summary."  # 640f
    fields: {}  # 640f
- op: discuss  # 1a88
  at: '2026-10-01T01:07:28Z'  # 1a88
  by: agent  # 1a88
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1a88
  clock: 2  # 1a88
  nonce: 1a88  # 1a88
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES.\nMechanism holds: profile.py _detect_languages (:871-922) counts every file the language's find_files / extension glob enumerates; excludes = DEFAULT_EXCLUDES + extra only; no is_test_file filter (profile.py uses is_test_file only for manifest/framework detection, :965, :1225). Spec hypergumbo-spec.md:1098 defines languages[L].files as \"the count of files the language-L analyzer would enumerate\" -- so per-contract, as the item says.\nNumbers drifted (self-survey of this repo at 134a06d505): profile.languages now has 23 languages (was 18). Classifying each language's node paths with hypergumbo_core.paths.is_test_file: 12 languages are 100% test-path -- csharp 2/2, elixir 1/1, erlang 1/1, go 4/4, java 3/3, php 1/1, proto 1/1, solidity 1/1, sql 1/1, swift 3/3, wgsl 1/1, xml 1/1 -- plus ruby (1 profile file, 0 nodes). Non-test-backed: python, typescript, javascript, html (packages/htrac-frontend), bash, json, yaml, toml, markdown, rust (10 non-test paths, under packages/hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer/recorded/, not test-classified).\nCONSTRAINT THE FIX MUST RESPECT: the WI-jadig file-presence pre-filter skips any analyzer whose languages read files == 0 in profile.languages (spec :1373). Dropping test-fixture files from languages[L].files would stop those analyzers running on the fixtures. A fix has to ADD a field (e.g. a per-language non-test count, or a test share) rather than shrink `files`.\nProposed update: refresh 18 -> 23 and the per-language list; add the pre-filter constraint to the description. INV-nohod (the related item) is satisfied."  # 1a88
