  set:  # 9c29
    title: "profile.languages presents a 23-language polyglot; 12 of those languages come only from test fixtures"  # 9c29
    description: "**Defect.** The language-composition summary presents the repository as a broad polyglot, where most of the extra languages come only from test fixtures.\n\n**Evidence.** On a self-analysis map of this repo (dev 134a06d505), `profile.languages` reports 23 languages. Twelve are backed only by test-path files (hypergumbo_core.paths.is_test_file): csharp 2/2, elixir 1/1, erlang 1/1, go 4/4, java 3/3, php 1/1, proto 1/1, solidity 1/1, sql 1/1, swift 3/3, wgsl 1/1, xml 1/1 — plus ruby (1 profile file, 0 nodes). Most come from tests/fixtures/schema-coverage-corpus/<lang>/ and packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/fixtures/. The application is a Python+TypeScript project (plus bash/json/yaml/toml/markdown config and docs). `_detect_languages` (profile.py:871-922) counts every file a language's find_files / extension glob enumerates, excluding only DEFAULT_EXCLUDES; there is no test-file exclusion.\n\n**Contract.** A \"what is this written in?\" composition summary should reflect the real codebase composition, or document that fixture languages are included. (Note: spec hypergumbo-spec.md:1098 defines languages[L].files as \"the count of files the language-L analyzer would enumerate\" with no test exclusion, so this is per-contract — weak/borderline.)\n\n**Constraint on the fix.** The WI-jadig file-presence pre-filter skips any analyzer whose languages read files == 0 in profile.languages (spec :1373). Dropping test-fixture files from languages[L].files would stop those analyzers running on the fixtures. The fix must ADD a field (e.g. a per-language non-test file count or test share) rather than shrink `files`.\n\n**Consequence.** A consumer asking what languages the project uses is told it uses a dozen extra languages (incl. Solidity/WGSL/Swift) that appear only as test fixtures — a misleading picture of the technology stack.\n\n**Related (not duplicate).** Adjacent to INV-nohod (test-dominated node count, satisfied) but a distinct surface: the codebase-composition summary.\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 9c29
- op: discuss  # e4fb
